{"duration_api_ms":159954,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3fd8b4c4-ccec-45df-a8d3-b4f3c09a8479","total_cost_usd":0.217808,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15581,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15548,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10736},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15581,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15548,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15581,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15581},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15548,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15581,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.217808,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":10736,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The front is a one-dimensional gamma sweep at a single geometry corner: D=3.384, b=1.2, cone=70. Peak heat flux runs 227k to 275k W/m2 and bondline temperature 418 K to 391 K. The steep end is capped by max_g at gamma of about -3.57 deg. D is capped by heatshield mass fraction (margin 0.00074 at D=3.384). b is capped at about 1.2 by the cd_fore surrogate hull, and cone is capped at 70 deg by the variable bound. No other region of the data comes close to the front. Small or blunt-poor designs have flux of 330k to 1.7M W/m2 and are dominated. I therefore spend this round on filling gamma gaps at a marginally larger D, and I rely on data-fitted local sensitivities rather than new physics.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-92f6aed905e3 through C-f71f4a44911d: same D, b and cone with gamma from -1.5 to -3.565. Flux rises about 12k per deg and T falls about 10 K per deg. g reaches 11.991 at -3.565, a margin of 0.00078.\",\"Heatshield mass margin is 0.0007356 at D=3.384 (C-f71f4a44911d) and 0.003097 at D=3.38 (C-3976a1ed5e2c). That slope puts the D limit near 3.3852.\",\"C-fbfc374c65e1 (D=3.36, cone 69.5) gives 263720 W/m2 at gamma -3, against 260980 for the corner. This matches flux proportional to D^-1.5 with almost no cone effect. T is about 19 K per m of D, so a slightly larger D is a small gain in both objectives.\",\"C-ea8a7098ba1b (b=1.15, D=3.37) has higher flux and T and only a slightly larger mass margin. Lower b is therefore worse.\",\"C-425c523a5086, C-5b57439845df, C-e605b64e0636 and C-3d41ce848a30 (b of 1.21 to 1.25 at cone 70) fail the cd_fore hull. C-c708a99f10f1, C-17a9b770e63c and C-a55828a3ab03 (cone 62 to 67) fail on geometry. Neither corner can be pushed further.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak flux follows a Sutton-Graves-like law (prior knowledge). It falls with nose radius b*D and rises with ballistic coefficient, giving roughly D^-1.5 in the data. Bondline temperature follows heat load, which falls with steeper entry and larger D. Larger D is limited by the mass fraction, larger b by the surrogate hull, and steeper gamma by max_g. The design is boxed in at D=3.3848, b=1.2, cone=70, so the only free direction is gamma. The D increase from 3.384 to 3.3845 or 3.3848 is a tiny but dominating improvement, kept inside the estimated mass-fraction limit.\",\"uncertainty\":\"The mass-fraction margin at D=3.3845 to 3.3848 is a linear extrapolation of about 0.0004 to 0.0003. It could be slightly nonlinear, so I keep D no higher than 3.3848. The gamma interpolations are accurate to about 0.3 K and 0.3%. The g margin near gamma -3.567 is thin, at about 0.0005 by extrapolation. I have no data on how the hull behaves at b above 1.2 with cone below 70, so I do not probe it here.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-92f6aed905e3\",\"rationale\":\"Shallow end of the front at a marginally larger D, which slightly dominates the parent.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3848,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227270,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks the D increase and the mass margin at the shallow end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-92f6aed905e3\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -1.5 and -1.65.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3845,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.575},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":228750,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.67,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front near the shallow end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1120f80f8763\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate the front between gamma -1.65 and -1.8 at slightly larger D.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3845,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":231250,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":414.63,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-5bc54b8cbb1b\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate the front between gamma -1.65 and -1.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3845,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.75},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":232300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.83,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills a front gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6a031c8b7ef2\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.0 and -2.25.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3845,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":239900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":408.56,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the largest gap in the mid-front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-6a031c8b7ef2\",\"rationale\":\"Second point in the -2.0 to -2.25 gap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3845,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.17},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":241500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the same gap and checks smoothness.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8f904ab2a396\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.0 and -2.25.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3845,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.2},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":242130,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":407.13,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Fills the same gap.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-8f904ab2a396\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.25 and -2.375.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3845,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.74,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-5a0e298559c0\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.375 and -2.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3845,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.43},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":247500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-f8e103c54279\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -2.5 and -2.625 at D=3.3848.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3848,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":250240,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":402.41,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the largest safe D at mid-front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-a105e67a2af3\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.625 and -2.75.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3845,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.69},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":253700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.6,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-271015a622de\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.75 and -2.875.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3845,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.81},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":256500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":399.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-971126c8c2f3\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -2.875 and -3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3845,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.95},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":259740,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.57,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-4da368065e68\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gap between gamma -3.0 and -3.125.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3845,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.05},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":262130,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.47,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densifies the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7566ad6198e4\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate between gamma -3.125 and -3.25 at D=3.3848.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diame